# [DD-13b.W1.2] A `target` NAMING A DEFINITION THE FILE DOES NOT DECLARE.
#
# §1.3's refusal table, tier 2: name the definition AND the `lib` chain
# that was searched, so an author can tell "I misspelled it" from "it
# lives in a library and this build cannot reach into one yet". W1.2 has
# no composer, so the second is a real and common case rather than a
# hypothetical.
#
# W1.1 COULD NOT SEE THIS AT ALL — it parsed `target` and resolved
# nothing — which is how the head_basic fixture came to name a
# definition that did not exist for a whole step without anything going
# red.
target t = level_filter

pattern a+
name something_else
m "aaa" 0 3
